.he "ncheck (1)                 8/16/26                   ncheck (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
ncheck
- print the names that correspond to inumbers
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
ncheck [ -av ] [ -i inumber ... ] filesystem
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Ncheck walks the directories of the named file system and prints, for
each directory entry, the inumber and the path that reaches it.
With no -i, every entry is printed; with -i, only the entries whose
inumber is named.
.sp
It is the way to find which file an inode is, which is what you want
after icheck or dcheck has complained about one by number.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
OPTIONS
.in +5
.br
.in +10
.ti -10
-a	Print the . and .. entries, which are otherwise left out.

.ti -10
-v	Be verbose.

.ti -10
-i inumber	Print only the entry or entries that name inumber.

.in -10
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
icheck (1), dcheck (1)
